    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive alignment, headlined by **Yordan Alvarez** (78.68) and **Junior Caminero** (76.88), our two highest-scoring options. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start against Flaherty given his elite 0.444 xwOBA, while **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Kelly, whose 4.85 xERA presents a prime opportunity to drive up our counting stats. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused strategy; **Trea Turner** (68.26) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.03) are clear starts. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** faces a tougher arm in Woodruff, his projection is bolstered by a massive 14% dynamic platoon boost and the high likelihood of a stolen base against a slow-working delivery. **Kyle Schwarber** also provides excellent leverage at a 67.89 score, serving as a high-floor anchor alongside **Trea Turner** at the top of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s bench involved **Jacob Gonzalez** (44.32), who fell just shy of our rotation requirements. While **Jacob Gonzalez** projects as a viable utility piece, his position at the bottom of the order (-8% adjustment) dragged his efficiency below the threshold of our primary starters. We also observed a notable platoon surge for **Lars Nootbaar** (61.85), whose 11% dynamic platoon edge against Phillips solidifies his status as a recommended start despite the neutral park conditions. Conversely, we are keeping **Dillon Dingler** (36.48) and **Carson Benge** (37.03) sidelined; both fell below our 40.0 efficiency floor due to unfavorable matchups against Brown and Luzardo, respectively. We continue to monitor the status of **Rece Hinds**, who remains in the minors, and we will avoid any unnecessary game cap burn by keeping **Colt Keith** (52.08) in a limited role, given the suppression of his ceiling by the elite hold capability of his opposing pitcher.",
